# .claude/worktree-deps — worktree-mode marker for {{PROJECT_NAME}}.
#
# Its presence puts this project in worktree mode: /plan and /code give each
# concurrent session its own copy of the repo under .claude/worktrees/<branch>,
# so two sessions can never share a working tree or switch each other's branch.
# /merge tears the worktree down after the PR lands.
#
# Listed below are this stack's heavy git-ignored runtime paths. link-deps.sh
# SYMLINKS each one from the main checkout into every new worktree, so the app
# runs there without a second install and .env copies cannot drift. A path that
# does not exist yet (before a first install) is a warning, not an error.
#
# One path per line; blank lines and # comments are ignored.
# node_modules is linked, never copied — one install serves every worktree.
# .next is linked so a worktree does not rebuild the whole cache cold.

.env
.env.local
node_modules
.next
